config-connector-extensions patch 0047: the direct reconciler requeues a
refusal for quota and never marks the object failed.

A cloud API's refusal for quota (HTTP 429, gRPC RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED) says
"not now", not "this object is wrong". The direct reconciler treated it as
any other error: UpdateFailed or DeleteFailed (Ready False), then the
workqueue's backoff from 250 ms, which against a per-minute quota made
more refused requests (live: DataplexLake, DataplexZone and DataplexAsset
under Dataplex's 10 requests a minute per user and region; IAMAccessPolicy
under GetAccessPolicy's 5 a minute per project). With Deps.QuotaBackoff
set, handleUpdateFailed and handleDeleteFailed leave the status alone for
such an error, and Reconcile requeues the object after
QuotaBackoff(refusals in a row), records a QuotaExhausted warning event,
and forgets the count on the next success. Unset, nothing changes.
directbase/quota.go is new: IsQuotaExhausted (googleapi.Error 429,
apierror.APIError, a gRPC status) and the per-object count.
Upstream candidate: yes.

